     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>From what I can tell, the problem relates to the draws from truncated distributions: that the support of the truncated distributions need to fully overlap with the constraints on the parameters. The problem is then that yStar is unconstrained, but the draws are from a truncated distribution. I see that Bob Carpenter has noted this a number of times in his responses to others.</div><div><br></div><div>So, in the end, I think I just need to constrain the parameters yStar to be between the relevant cut points kappa at each iteration.</div><div><br></div><div>By example, in a model with a single cut point:</div><div><br></div><div>If y_i = 1, constrain yStar_i to be less than kappa,</div><div>If y_i = 2, constrain yStar_i to be greater than kappa</div><div><br></div><div>The constraint thus depends on the value(s) of kappa drawn at a given iteration. Can I do this in the transformed parameter or model block? Is there another way to do this?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank again!</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br>On Friday, March 11, 2016 at 2:31:16 PM UTC-5, Gregory wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello everyone,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m putting together an auto-regressive ordered logistic regression model, where the interpretation relates to the value of the latent variable yStar.</div><div><br></div><div>At the latent-variable level, the model is the following: yStar_t ~ logistic(beta * x1 + rho * yStar_{t -1}, 1)</div><div><br></div><div>At the observed-variable level: y_t ~ ordered_logistic(beta * x1 + rho * yStar_{t -1}, kappa)</div><div><br></div><div>I started with the simplest version of this model: a single cut point and a single covariate.<br></div><div><br></div><div>I set the model up in Stan in two steps:</div><div><br></div><div>(1) draws are made from the posterior for the values of yStar using a truncated logistic density: given the observed value of y, the latent variable yStar is known to be within a given range as defined by the cut point parameters</div><div><br></div><div>(2) ordered_logistic() is used to estimate the regression of interest for the observed variable</div><div><br></div><div>The problem is that I get the following error and I seem to have run out of ideas for where I&#39;m going wrong:</div><div><br></div><div><div>[299] &quot;  Log probability evaluates to log(0), i.e. negative infinity.&quot;                                       </div><div>[300] &quot;  Stan can&#39;t start sampling from this initial value.&quot;                                                 </div><div>[301] &quot;Initialization between (--2, -2) failed after 100 attempts. &quot;                                         </div><div>[302] &quot; Try specifying initial values, reducing ranges of constrained values, or reparameterizing the model.&quot;</div></div><div><br></div><div>Any suggestions for would great!</div><div><br></div><div>Simulation and model code:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rstan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>n_obs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_obs<br>x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Covariate</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>beta1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Parameter on covariate x1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>rho </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Auto-regressive parameter</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>kappa </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Cut points</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>k </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Number of cut points</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>S </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yStar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Simulate first-order auto-regressive ordinal logistic regression data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Generate latent (linear) variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    S$yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Arbitrary set yStar for t = 1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    S$yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rho </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S$yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  beta1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  rlogis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Generate observed (ordered) variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S$yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S$yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S$y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> i<br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model_data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_obs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_obs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S$y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S$year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> S$x1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<br>data {<br><br>  int n_obs;<br><br>  int y[n_obs];<br>  int year[n_obs];<br>  real x1[n_obs];<br><br>}<br><br>parameters {<br>  <br>  vector[n_obs] yStar; # Latent variable<br>  real rho; # Auto-regression parameter<br>  <br>  vector[1] beta; # Standard covariate parameters<br>  ordered[1] kappa; # Cut points<br><br>}<br><br>transformed parameters {<br>}<br><br>model {<br><br>  // Priors<br>  rho ~ normal(0, 5);<br>  <br>  beta ~ normal(0, 5);<br>  kappa ~ normal(0, 5);<br><br>  // Prior on first latent variable<br>  if(y[1] == 1) yStar[1] ~ normal(0, 5) T[, kappa[1]];<br>  if(y[1] == 2) yStar[1] ~ normal(0, 5) T[kappa[1], ];<br><br>  // Draws for yStar<br>  for(t in 2:n_obs) {<br><br>    if(y[t] == 1) {<br>      yStar[t] ~ logistic(rho * yStar[t - 1] +<br>                          beta[1] * x1[t],<br>                          1) T[, kappa[1]];<br>    }<br>    if(y[t] == 2) {<br>      yStar[t] ~ logistic(rho * yStar[t - 1] +<br>                          beta[1] * x1[t],<br>                          1) T[kappa[1], ];<br>    }<br>  }<br><br>  // Likelihood<br>  for(t in 2:n_obs) {<br>    y[t] ~ ordered_logistic(rho * yStar[t - 1] + beta[1] * x1[t], kappa);<br>  }<br>}<br><br>generated quantities {<br>}&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Compile to C</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model_latent </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan_model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_code</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Sample from posterior</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>posterior_latent </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sampling</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_latent</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                             warmup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                             open_progress </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cK61yLPmBgAJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2016-03-12T18:40:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: Auto-regressive ordered logistic regression",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Greg,</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Saturday, March 12, 2016 at 1:01:02 PM UTC-5, Gregory wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">The\r\n constraint thus depends on the value(s) of kappa drawn at a given \r\niteration. Can I do this in the transformed parameter or model block? Is\r\n there another way to do this?</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div> <br>kappa proposed, not kappa drawn<br><br>It can be done but you have to account for the change-of-variables and such models tend not to mix well.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">parameters</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  pos_ordered</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">J </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     // be sure to estimate this intercept since kappa is positive<br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> {<br>      yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      increment_log_prob(log(kappa[1]));<br>    }<br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> J</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> {<br>      real diff;<br>      diff &lt;- </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];<br></span></code>       yStar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">diff</span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></code>;<br>      increment_log_prob(log(diff));<br>    }<br>    else {<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">      yStar[i] &lt;- </span><span style=\"color:#000\">kappa[J] / (</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><span style=\"color:#660\"><code><span style=\"color:#000\">1 - u[i])</span></code></span></code>;<br>      increment_log_prob(log(kappa[j]) + 2 * log1m(u[i]));<br>    }<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ujer1aPyBgAJ",
   "from": "Gregory",
